ure of chilean spanish is  the use of the prefix they to emphasize  or intensify adjectives here's a  standard spanish sentence meaning this  game is really difficult  in chilean spanish you might hear este  huevos  notice that the prefix re is used  instead of muy  vocabulary some of the vocabulary used  in chile is not completely exclusive to  chile but is used in certain other latin  american countries as well for example  in chile the usual word for car is  which is also used in argentina bolivia  ecuador paraguay peru and uruguay the  word used in most other parts of latin  america is caro while koche is used in  spain  in chile the word for bus specifically  an inter-city bus is mikro this word is  also used in argentina as well as in  mexico city with the meaning of minibus  in other countries words like altobus  cameon or omnibus are used  in chile the word for computer is  computador a word that's also used in  colombia but in most other places in  latin america the usual word is  computadora in spain the word is  ordinador  some words are used exclusively or  almost exclusively in chilean spanish in  chile the word for light bulb is an  the most common word outside of chile is  bombilla which refers to a drinking  straw in chile  in chile the word for a t-shirt is  bolera outside of chile the usual word  is camiseta in chile this refers to an  undershirt rather than a t-shirt  in chile a baseball cap is referred to  as a joki outside of chile the usual  word is gora or gora de basibol  there are a number of words for toilet  in the spanish language one of them  being retrete the chilean spanish word  is what or alternatively  literally bowl of the bathroom  one special element of chilean spanish  vocabulary is its loan words from  indigenous languages which are normally  used in addition to native spanish words  with a similar meaning the general  spanish word for baby is baby in chilean  spanish there's the word  which comes from the quechua and imada  word for baby  this is also used in bolivia ecuador and  some parts of colombia and peru  in general spanish the word for  boyfriend is novio and the word for  girlfriend is novia the chilean spanish  words are polulo for boyfriend and  polola for girlfriend estes mi polola  carla this is my girlfriend carla these  words come from the mapudengun word  pyulyu which means acting like a fly as  in the insect the meaning comes from the  metaphor of a fly hovering around a  fruit the way a man or woman hovers  around their desired partner  another word of mapo moon origin is  which means little or short in the sense  of quantity like poco  i have little juice left this comes from  the maputhangun word piccintun  the word for belly  me  this means my belly hurts or i have a  stomachache  the word meaning gossip  i've got some gossip to tell you this  word comes from the maputhalun word  kawin meaning party the word was used to  refer to a type of meeting where the  heads of different tribes gather  together to discuss various issues  concerning their region but also to  socialize and gossip that's why it's now  used with the meaning of gossip  there's also chilean spanish slang as  you might expect some of it's used in  other latin american countries as well  such as magan this means cool or awesome  in addition to chile it's also used in  ecuador peru colombia and cuba  this car is cool  i had a great time at the beach where i  had a fun time at the beach  but some slang is specifically chilean  altitude this means right now or right  away  come to my house right now  it's used with an imperative or with an  answer to an imperative it literally  means as the shot is fired so it's like  saying as fast as a bullet  yeah in general spanish this means now  in chilean slang it's used as an answer  to a command and it shows agreement in a  similar way to okay for example this  exchange meaning do your homework okay  okay let's do this in this case it's  used as an answer to a co